  "description": "EKOLIC crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R 3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C120 H99 Cd3 N6 O27 Sm3,3(C1 H4 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 10 O neighbors; Cd1 (Cd) has 4 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 10 O neighbors; Cd2 (Cd) has 4 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 10 O neighbors; Cd3 (Cd) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.754-4.975 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.27-171.98°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Cd3Sm3L3(OAc)6(OH)3]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
